            <ArticleTitle>Splenic decapsulation after gastroscopy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>282-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00508-012-0158-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sanguineous splenic complications in elective treatment procedures remain a potentially life-threatening complication in patients of all age groups. In this case, the patient, as per her past medical history, underwent a laparoscopic appendectomy when she was admitted to the clinic. One of the diagnostic procedures to find the reason for the epigastric pain, a gastroscopy, can retrospectively be held responsible for decapsulation of the spleen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
